  "needs_manual_review": true,
  "needs_manual_review_reason": "Series-level GEO metadata verified directly against the live source; per-sample clinical/pathology fields (grade, sex/age, anatomic location, brain invasion, treatment timepoint) have not yet been extracted from individual GSM records or supplementary tables. FACT-CHECK UPDATE (2026-07-10 verification pass): date_deposited/date_updated filled in from the live GEO record's Series_submission_date/Series_last_update_date, previously 'Not reported'. FACT-CHECK UPDATE (2026-07-12 re-verification pass): raw_data_available corrected from 'Not reported' to true; the live series lists GSE189521_RAW.tar (raw IDAT array files) as a supplementary_file entry. Confirmed all 110 GSMs carry only tissue='meningioma tumor' at the GSM level (grade/sex/age live only in the GSE189521_Clinical_data.xlsx supplement, not in GSM metadata), so those demographic fields remain 'Not reported' at the GEO metadata level. DEEP-AUDIT UPDATE (2026-07-14): re-fetched the live GSE189521 family.soft fresh: 110 GSM records confirmed (matches sample_count), all 110 carrying only 'tissue: meningioma tumor' at the GSM level (grade/sex/age genuinely absent from GSM metadata, confirmed again), raw IDAT (Grn/Red) files present per sample (raw_data_available=true still correct), and Series_supplementary_file still lists GSE189521_Clinical_data.xlsx (processed_data_format correct) alongside GSE189521_RAW.tar and a methylation sample sheet. related_accessions (GSE189673 SuperSeries, GSE189672 RNA-seq subseries) reconfirmed via the live GSE189673 Series_relation fields ('SuperSeries of: GSE189521' and 'SuperSeries of: GSE189672', no other subseries exists, so no WES GEO series was missed despite GSE189672's own overall_design text mentioning WES was also performed on this cohort -- that WES data, if deposited, is not under a GEO accession found via this SuperSeries). Publication PMID 35108039 re-confirmed via PubMed esummary (title/venue/year/authors match exactly) and its PMC copy (PMC11313601). One genuine error found and fixed: corresponding_author was listed as 'James C Bayley, Akash J Patel' -- Bayley is the GEO submission contact (Series_contact_name = 'James,Cushing,Bayley') and the paper's first author, not a corresponding author. Directly reading the PMC11313601 full text shows the paper itself explicitly designates three corresponding authors via asterisked footnote: 'Corresponding author. Email: akash.patel@bcm.edu (A.J.P.); klisch@bcm.edu (T.J.K.); akdes.serinharmanci@bcm.edu (A.S.H.)' -- i.e. Akash J Patel, Tiemo J Klisch, and Akdes S Harmanci, not Bayley. Corrected corresponding_author to list all three true corresponding authors per the paper's own designation. DEEP-AUDIT UPDATE 2 (2026-07-14): the prior passes' note that 'per-sample clinical/pathology fields... have not yet been extracted' from GSE189521_Clinical_data.xlsx turned out to be leaving substantial genuinely-available data on the table -- this pass downloaded and directly opened that supplement (ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE189nnn/GSE189521/suppl/GSE189521_Clinical_data.xlsx, confirmed still listed as a live Series_supplementary_file) with openpyxl. It is a per-sample table for all 110 samples (Sample, MenG, Gender, Age, MIB, WHO grade, Brain Invasion, Necrosis, Location, Simpson_grade, ResectionType, Recurrence, MonthsFollowUp, WES/RNA-seq/Methylation availability, PLS, Ch1pLoss, Ch22Loss, TotalChrDeletions, NF2_LogExp, and per-gene mutation columns for NF2/SMARCB1/TRAF7/KLF4/AKT1/PIK3CA/SMO/POLR2A/ARID1A, TERT Promoter Mutation), not just an abstract-level claim -- so, unlike the Hertie/gse-292325/Mendeley false-positive pattern this project has documented elsewhere, this is the opposite situation: real per-sample data was sitting unextracted behind a 'Not reported'/false placeholder. Corrections made from direct tabulation of this table: grade_breakdown filled in from the 'WHO grade' column (90 WHO I, 20 WHO II, 0 WHO III, sums to 110); brain_invasion.status_reported set true with counts '0 of 110 positive' (all 110 rows explicitly marked 'N', not merely absent from the table) and determination_method left 'Not reported' since no method is stated (tags.brain_invasion_annotated correctly stays false per the schema's determination-method requirement); sex_distribution filled in from 'Gender' (67 F, 43 M); age_distribution filled in from 'Age' (range 19-81, mean 57.8, n=110); anatomic_location_breakdown filled in from 'Location' (17 distinct sites tallied, see field); molecular_subtype_annotated (top-level and tag) corrected from 'Not reported'/false to true -- the 'MenG' column assigns each sample to a named DNA-methylation-based subtype (MenG A: 52, MenG B: 26, MenG C: 22, Unknown: 10, sums to 110), which is exactly the 'DNA methylation class' example given in docs/schema.md's own tag definition, and is a genuine per-sample annotated classification, not merely the paper's topic/title; has_outcome_data (top-level and tag) corrected from 'Not reported'/false to true -- the 'Recurrence' (91 N / 19 Y) and 'MonthsFollowUp' (0 to 96.5 months, n=110) columns are genuine deposited per-sample recurrence-free-survival data, checked carefully against this project's own documented Hertie/gse-292325/Mendeley overreach pattern before accepting: this is not an abstract's prognostic framing, it is an actual data column with a value for every sample. tags.recurrence_annotated deliberately left false and not touched: the 'Recurrence' column records each patient's subsequent clinical recurrence outcome, not a primary-vs-recurrent-specimen sample-type distinction (all 110 samples are primary-tumor specimens per the series' own overall_design 'DNA methylation... of 110 primary meningiomas'), which is a different concept per the schema's own definition ('distinguishes primary vs. recurrent samples with counts') -- so this does not qualify. tags.grade_comparable corrected false to true given the now-established explicit per-grade breakdown. treatment_timepoint_status intentionally left 'Not reported': no explicit pre/post-radiation or treatment-naive field exists in this table. SAMPLE-LEVEL TABLE ADDED (2026-07-14): re-downloaded the same GSE189521_Clinical_data.xlsx fresh (byte-identical to the GSE189672 sibling's copy, confirming both subseries share one clinical annotation file) and parsed all 110 rows into the new optional `samples` field (one row per sample: sample_id, sex, age, who_grade, anatomic_location, outcome [Recurrence + MonthsFollowUp], molecular_subtype [MenG group]) -- this is the pilot for a new per-sample browsing table feature on the website, modeled on the ScPCA Portal's sample-level pages. This is genuine per-sample source data, not derived/estimated from the aggregate counts already in this record. ONTOLOGY ADDED (2026-07-14): disease_id=MONDO:0016642, tissue_ids=['UBERON:0003547'], both verified live against the EBI Ontology Lookup Service (ols4/api/search) before use, not guessed. Generic term, same reasoning as its GSE189672 sibling (same 110-patient cohort).",
